==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*eri}}, derived from {{m|urj-fin-pro|*erä}} (see {{m|fi|erä}} for more). Cognate with {{cog|et|eri}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Adjective===
{{fi-adj}} {{tlb|fi|not comparable|indeclinable}}

# [[different]], [[other]], [[another]]
#: {{coi|fi|olla '''eri''' mieltä (jonkun kanssa)|to [[disagree]] (with somebody)}}
#: {{coi|fi|'''eri''' tavalla|in a [[different]] [[manner]], in a different [[way]]}}
#: {{coi|fi|'''eri''' tavoin|in [[different]]/[[many]] [[manner]]s, in different/many [[way]]s}}
#: {{ux|fi|Se on '''eri''' sana.|That's a '''different''' / an'''other''' word.}}
# [[different]], [[separate]]

====Inflection====
The cases of ''eri'' are used only as adverbs.
{{fi-decl-pron|1s=[[eri]]|8p=[[erillään]]|10p=[[erilleen]]|12p=[[erikseen]]|a8p=[[erittäin]]}}

In colloquial language, ''eri'' may sometimes be inflected as a regular adjective. This is considered nonstandard.
{{fi-decl-risti|pos=adj|er|||ä}}

